  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I went through all 7 patients on 'DOAC dose review - week of 10/19/2026' under RBC-PHARM-07. Six doses ended up changed and one stayed the same. Each change has a signed progress note citing the results, orders and letters it relied on.\n\n1. **pt-0061 Castellano:** apixaban raised from 2.5 to **5 mg twice daily** (mr-t0001). She meets none of the three dose criteria, and the St. Brigid letter of 9/10 says her itraconazole course ended on 8/14.\n2. **pt-0003 Delgado:** **no net change; stays on rivaroxaban 20 mg daily** (mr-t0013). I first lowered him to 15 mg based on St. Brigid's creatinine of 160 µmol/L. During the review the lab corrected it to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL) because of an analyzer calibration fault. That gives CrCl 59.9, so I put him back on 20 mg and wrote a correction note.\n3. **pt-0041 Duquette:** apixaban lowered from 5 to **2.5 mg twice daily** (mr-t0005). He meets no criteria, but he is taking itraconazole (an interacting drug under the policy), which Dr. Sorensen started 10/6.\n4. **pt-0062 Fairweather:** apixaban lowered from 5 to **2.5 mg twice daily** (mr-t0014). He meets two criteria: age 82, and a creatinine of 150 µmol/L (1.70 mg/dL) from his St. Brigid ED visit on 10/21, which arrived during the review.\n5. **pt-0038 Moravec:** rivaroxaban raised from 15 to **20 mg daily** (mr-t0007). His May dose cut used ideal body weight; the policy requires actual weight. With his measured 96 kg, CrCl is 56.1.\n   - He sent a portal message during the review reporting 185 lb on his home scale. The policy doesn't count a reported weight, so the decision stands.\n   - At that weight his CrCl would be about 49, which would call for 15 mg. I created a task for RN triage (task-t0024) to get a measured clinic weight.\n6. **pt-0043 Pellegrino:** rivaroxaban lowered from 20 to **15 mg daily** (mr-t0009). Her creatinine from 10/22 came back at 1.25 mg/dL during the review, giving CrCl 43.6.\n7. **pt-0002 Vance:** **no net change; stays on apixaban 2.5 mg twice daily** (mr-t0015). He meets only one criterion (age 82; weight 64.9 kg, creatinine 1.21), so I first raised him to 5 mg. A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived showing itraconazole started 10/22 for 12 weeks. I lowered him back to 2.5 mg and wrote a correction note.\n\nNone of the cases fell under the policy rule that requires telling the prescriber. No other medications were changed. I closed the five items that arrived in the inbox during the review with comments, and both queues were clear of new items at the end.\n\nFor your follow-up: pt-0041 and pt-0002 are on the lower dose only because of itraconazole. Their apixaban dose should be rechecked when each 12-week course ends (about 2027-01-14 for pt-0002).",
